{"name":"Pimm’s","hex":"#c3585c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Pimm's","blocks":[{"text":"Pimm's is an English brand of gin-based fruit cup but may also be considered a liqueur or the basis of a sling or punch. It was first produced in 1823 by James Pimm and has been owned by Diageo since 1997. Its most popular product is Pimm's No. 1 Cup, commonly used for the Pimm's cup cocktail."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Pimm%27s_Cup.jpg/330px-Pimm%27s_Cup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pimm's","wikidata":"Q1761185"},{"title":"Pimm","blocks":[{"text":"Pimm is a surname, and may refer to:"},{"items":["Ed Pimm, American racing driver","Jack Pimm (1920–2016), Australian rules footballer","James Pimm (1798–1866), English caterer, inventor of Pimm's liqueur","Jerry Pimm, American basketball coach","Pat Pimm (1957–2024), Canadian politician","Stuart Pimm, American ecologist","William Pimm (1864–1952), British sport shooter"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pimm","wikidata":"Q37456517"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Pimms_No_1_Cup_-_glass.jpg/500px-Pimms_No_1_Cup_-_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Pimms_No_1_Cup_-_glass.jpg/500px-Pimms_No_1_Cup_-_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pimm's and lemonade with mint sprigs and fruit","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APimms_No_1_Cup_-_glass.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Anyone_for_Pimm%27s%5E_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1398484.jpg/500px-Anyone_for_Pimm%27s%5E_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1398484.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/